# port-patches.sh: glm/series @ 14e8577b6303 over glm/zig-engine-base @ 0db3e2f6652b (commits 97c4f8e0f0f3..6f3edbfe37f4); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: KV shard host side: the part planner and pool parts, switches and their agreement, storage, placement check and telemetry (port of GLM 0118, parts 1-2)

KV sharding as GLM's Python 0118 designs it, not the DeepSeek port's lanes:
only the 11 DSA layers' 528-byte FP8 latent rows are sharded, each stream's on
the rank that owns its part of the pool; the pooled index keys stay pool-wide
on both ranks, so the token selection runs replicated, and the KDA states,
conv windows and index rings stay a slot's. This patch is the host side.

- cuda_pool: equal parts of whole extents, a part's end cutting its gaps;
  placement by part (fewer live streams, more free rows), twins in another
  part for prompt borrowing, moves that keep their part unless asked,
  segments and compaction steps around pinned twins, a layout digest.
- cuda_shard: the part sizes and addresses, the decode glue, the history
  fetch's model, the crossing rows; the switches and their refusals.
- Storage: each latent plane holds a part plus trash rows; the other rank's
  extent has no latent rows here (a view without them is refused where
  latent rows would be written or copied); the display reserve holds this
  rank's owner planes first; the sharded pool is sized in the unsharded
  pool's agreed memory and agreed again; a part shorter than --context
  shortens the served window (logged).
- Placement check: rank 1 places every extent itself, so rank 0 sends each
  prefill's placement (by base, rows, part and slot, never an id) and, every
  TF_GLM_KV_SHARD_CHECK decode rounds, its layout digest; a difference ends
  the pair.
- Telemetry: /health kv_shard (per_part, per_rank), /metrics
  tensorfold:kv_shard_* (core/lanes/kv_parts.zig, the DeepSeek port's).

Switches (both ranks, in the ranks' agreed settings text, nothing added when
off): TF_GLM_KV_SHARD (0; 1 on), TF_GLM_KV_SHARD_CARRY (1),
TF_GLM_KV_SHARD_TWINS (1: prompt borrowing; no decode twins),
TF_GLM_KV_SHARD_CHECK (decode rounds between the ranks' layout digests, 1024;
0 none). Refused after the agreement, on every rank alike, before NCCL: TP
other than 2, --parallel 1, MTP drafts, TF_GLM_MULTI_LONE=1. In this patch
TF_GLM_KV_SHARD=1 is refused at start ("KV sharding's GPU paths are not in
this build yet"): the KV shard patch turns it on. Off, the settings text, the
caches' layout, the segment table, the pool, the notes and /health are as
before (the pool with one part checked against a verbatim copy of the old pool
over 200 random sequences).

Tests: the Python fork's tools/kv_shard_check.py and kv_shard_mutants.sh as
Zig tests (cuda_shard_test.zig), the switches, the pool agreement, the
placement record and digest, the storage layout, the lane host's and the
server's telemetry.

Measured on the pair: nothing on its own (sharding is refused here); with the
KV shard patch see there.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo); GLM patch 0118,
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#152.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0020-zig-glm-kv-shard-host.patch

